nitro is back on team liquid and he had  a lot to say about his time in valorant  as well as his decision to return to  counter-strike so today we're coming at  you with a quick and juicy one about the  biggest player to ever return from the  valorant hinterlands at least so far  [Music]  grand slam winner legendary n a igl team  liquid fan favorite there are a lot of  ways you can describe nitro but valorent  pro is no longer among them on sunday  team liquid announced that nitro had  returned to their counter-strike roster  but it was hardly a surprise back in  november upcomers george gettys reported  that nitro was thinking about his future  and considering return to counter-strike  now in an interview with team liquid's  austin ryan nitro confirmed that he  hadn't made any decision until december  but now that he has returned we've got a  lot to talk about first his time invalid  nitro joined hundred thieves alongside  team liquid alumnus hiko and they put up  some pretty good results they won first  strike n a which was the biggest  tournament for the region up until that  point they also placed first at a later  challengers qualifier they also played  one of the most exciting series in the  game to date and if you missed our video  on it in our every second count series  you should go check that out but  basically their accomplishments weren't  exactly jumping off the page they were a  solid team with a wealth of experience  in the genre but true dominance wasn't  ever really in the conversation  especially once international play  became more common in that liquid  interview nitro also mentioned that  there were a couple players where he had  to be a little bit more hands-on than he  was used to and that was sort of a sore  spot and it seems like it was the pgl  major that reminded him of his love for  the game that gave him his career but  the question is now  how is this new look liquid going to  perform as we saw with the previous  incarnations of team liquid csgo  appearances can be deceiving they were  one of the weakest teams in the early  online era stringing together basically  nothing but losses except for their  first place win at esl pro league season  11 finals which of course had just been  moved online then nitro left in august  2020 twists went to phase and grimm and  fallen were brought in as replacements  the team still looked excellent on paper  but that incarnation failed to win any  legitimately big events though they did  have some podium finishes here or there  and the scariest part about it is that  it seems like there's still no answer to  the question of  why from the liquid interview with nitro  quote we want a grand slam on land then  we go lose to a nobody team online so  it's like what the hell's going on  liquid i don't know dude there's no  solution it's just how we are it's hard  it really is then the fans look at you  and they're like why don't you just play  the same it's not how it works so can  this new liquid team do any better well  elysian naf are obviously very familiar  with nitro but with oc as their new oper  and cs legend shocks joining the squad  it really remains to be seen it seems  doubtful that nitro would ever have to  micromanage shocks who has a storied  career in the game and has even tried  igling in the past oc on the other hand  is a 22 year old oper who you may know  from extra salt and while he put up some  pretty great results there it remains to  be seen how he'll integrate into a  roster with players that are this  accomplished and experienced nitro said  in the interview that he thinks a team  has top five potential but that they  might need some work to get there that  seems fair to me but since the online  era began team liquid's rosters have  seemed better than they've actually  played and now with everything that's  happening consistent land play seems far  from certain but there's one last thing  i want to talk about unlike many people  who enjoy the constant back and forth of  valorent vs cs dimitri i actually enjoy  both games and i think that nitro's time  invalorant has actually made him a  better cs player sure he's not going to  be jet dashing around inferno although  that would be pretty awesome if he could  somehow do that but think about it with  me for a moment he had to lead a team  with new players some of whom were very  new to competition he had to flex onto  the op yet to think about this game in  its infancy and he had to lead this team  through a difficult time and mostly  online there are opportunities for  growth there maybe you don't think that  this liquid roster is an instant major  contender or maybe you do but i think  we're gonna see a hungrier nitra than we  did in summer 2020 and if you're a fan  of nacs  that's a sight for sore eyes  by the way every time you do a canadian  or american accent it absolutely  destroys me like i'm trying to place  your accent but it's actually  in 16 different places or something  right because it's like it's got too  many like borrowed things from it  and yeah  yeah that's so i'm sure when i do  british accents like people people  probably like who are actually from the  uk are probably like yo that's not  like there's no place where someone  where a single person speaks british  like that like you know like there's no  way  sweet okay
 

